intimidate|frighten-pressure|VERB|make someone afraid or less confident|To make someone feel afraid or less confident, sometimes to influence their behaviour.|đe dọa; làm sợ; gây áp lực khiến mất tự tin|The aggressive questions intimidated the new speaker.|Những câu hỏi gay gắt khiến người diễn giả mới mất tự tin.|Transitive intimidate someone; intimidate someone into doing something names an action induced by pressure.|-
rugby|ball-sport|NOUN|team sport with an oval ball|A team sport in which players carry, pass, and kick an oval ball to score.|môn rugby; bóng bầu dục rugby|The school rugby team practised passing on the field.|Đội rugby của trường tập chuyền bóng trên sân.|Uncountable when naming the sport; a rugby match is countable. Rugby is distinct from American football.|0
sensitive|emotional|ADJECTIVE|easily affected by feelings or treatment|Easily affected by emotions, criticism, or how others behave.|nhạy cảm; dễ bị tổn thương về cảm xúc|She is sensitive to criticism about her artwork.|Cô ấy nhạy cảm với những lời phê bình về tác phẩm của mình.|Sensitive to names the cause of an emotional response; does not necessarily mean unreasonable.|0
sensitive|responsive|ADJECTIVE|responding to small changes|Able to detect or be affected by small changes or particular conditions.|nhạy; dễ bị tác động|The sensor is sensitive to small changes in light.|Cảm biến nhạy với những thay đổi nhỏ của ánh sáng.|Sensitive to identifies the stimulus; the subject may be a device, material, or body part.|1
wise|good-judgment|ADJECTIVE|showing good judgment|Showing sound judgment based on understanding or experience.|khôn ngoan; sáng suốt|It was wise to check the route before leaving.|Kiểm tra lộ trình trước khi đi là một việc làm sáng suốt.|A wise decision or it is wise to do something evaluates judgment; not restricted to older people.|0
design|plan|NOUN|plan for how something will look or work|A plan showing how something should look, be built, or function.|bản thiết kế; thiết kế|The design includes a ramp beside the front steps.|Bản thiết kế có một lối dốc cạnh các bậc thềm phía trước.|Countable for a particular plan; uncountable for the activity or field of designing.|0
design|plan-and-create|VERB|plan the form or function of something|To plan the appearance, structure, or operation of something before it is made.|thiết kế|The students designed a box that could be folded flat.|Học sinh thiết kế một chiếc hộp có thể gấp phẳng.|Transitive design something; design something for a purpose identifies its intended use.|1
